From 73f36d2d25221df841e979e3996ee6e3438df21c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: kebab bring-up <local@invalid>
Date: Fri, 18 Sep 2026 13:58:40 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] kebab: front IMX471 is at slave address 0x10, not 0x1a

The 0084 powered scan on CCI1 master 1 found three devices:

  imx471 24-001a: DIAG(0084): 0x10 ACKED
  imx471 24-001a: DIAG(0084): 0x54 ACKED
  imx471 24-001a: DIAG(0084): 0x5c ACKED

0x54 and 0x5c are the front module's own EEPROM. 0x10 is the sensor. It
has never appeared in any earlier scan.

0x1a came from patch 0059 as the IMX family default and was never
confirmed for this board. The deep vendor-binary investigation on
2026-09-17 looked for a literal numeric address and did not find one, so
the default was left in place unchallenged. IMX sensors are commonly
strappable between 0x10 and 0x1a, and this module uses 0x10.

Every scan that could have caught this was disqualified for an unrelated
reason:

  0070  VANA inverted (0060), sensor unpowered; also master 0
  0075  VANA inverted, sensor unpowered; also master 0
  0079  correctly powered, but master 0 -- the GC5035 macro camera's bus

Only after 0077 fixed the VANA polarity, 0082 applied the vendor power
sequence and 0083 moved the node to the master the vendor devicetree
assigns, was a scan finally pointed at a powered sensor on the right bus.

This also retires the hardware-fault hypothesis. The module answers on
three addresses. It is present, powered and electrically healthy; the
0x50/0x58 EEPROM cited for two days as proof that "the bus is alive so
the sensor must be dead" belonged to a different camera on a different
bus.

Point the node at 0x10 and rename it camera@10 to match.
---
 .../boot/dts/qcom/sm8250-oneplus-kebab.dts    | 20 +++++++++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 18 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8250-oneplus-kebab.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8250-oneplus-kebab.dts
index 77ba5549e..b97e81442 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8250-oneplus-kebab.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8250-oneplus-kebab.dts
@@ -2062,9 +2062,25 @@ &cci1_i2c1 {
 	 */
 	clock-frequency = <400000>;
 
-	camf_imx471: camera@1a {
+	/*
+	 * Slave address 0x10, not 0x1a.
+	 *
+	 * The 0084 powered scan on CCI1 master 1 found three devices:
+	 *   0x10  <- this sensor
+	 *   0x54  ] the front module's own EEPROM
+	 *   0x5c  ]
+	 *
+	 * 0x1a was inherited from patch 0059 as the family default and was
+	 * never confirmed against this board. The vendor binaries never
+	 * exposed a literal address, and every scan that could have caught
+	 * 0x10 was disqualified: 0070 and 0075 ran with VANA inverted, and
+	 * 0079 ran on master 0, the GC5035's bus.
+	 *
+	 * IMX parts commonly strap between 0x10 and 0x1a.
+	 */
+	camf_imx471: camera@10 {
 		compatible = "sony,imx471";
-		reg = <0x1a>;
+		reg = <0x10>;
 
 		/* Vendor order VANA -> VDIG -> VIO; the driver enables these
 		 * in the order of its own supply table, not this one. */
-- 
